# OS/7 base system — installed on EVERY architecture, in every mode.
#
# The two architectures are different products:
#   amd64 - GUI or headless, chosen at install time. Adds the desktop from
#           package-lists-amd64/ and the Microsoft GUI stack from hooks-amd64/.
#   arm64 - SERVER ONLY. No GUI target, so no desktop list. os7-setup is
#           text-mode, so it installs this architecture too.
#
# README's "one shared package base" is per-architecture, so this split is
# consistent with it. Everything below is common to both.
#
# IMPORTANT: live-build package lists do NOT support trailing inline comments.
# Every token on a non-comment line is passed to apt as a package name.
# Keep comments on their own lines. (docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #9)

ubuntu-standard

# casper provides the Ubuntu live-boot init. live-build's ubuntu mode pulls it
# in by default, but naming it explicitly keeps the ISO's live-bootability from
# depending on a default. (docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #5)
casper

# --- Storage: ZFS root -------------------------------------------------------
# The GA-kernel-matched PREBUILT module, never zfs-dkms, so kernel and ZFS move
# in lockstep. Validated 2026-08-22: docs/SESSION-0-ZFS-VALIDATION.md
zfsutils-linux
zfs-initramfs

# The kernel. Do NOT swap this for a -virtual or -kvm flavour: those do not
# ship the ZFS module.
#
# linux-image-generic AND NOT linux-generic since 2026-08-25
# (docs/CURATION-AND-DELIVERY-PLAN.md §4.2). linux-generic is a two-line
# metapackage: linux-image-generic + linux-headers-generic. The headers exist to
# build DKMS modules and OS/7 has none to build - the ZFS module is the
# GA-kernel-matched PREBUILT one by locked decision.
#
# WHAT CARRIES THE ZFS MODULE, read out of the pinned archive's own index rather
# than reasoned about:
#   linux-generic       Depends: linux-image-generic, linux-headers-generic
#   linux-image-generic Depends: linux-image-<abi>-generic,
#                                linux-modules-<abi>-generic,
#                                linux-main-modules-zfs-<abi>-generic,
#                                linux-firmware
# So zfs.ko hangs off linux-image-generic and survives; only the headers leave.
# linux-modules-<abi>-generic is untouched, which is where the wireless drivers
# live - the thing this swap could plausibly have broken and does not.
linux-image-generic

# --- Identity: Entra ID login ------------------------------------------------
# authd is in the archive. Its Entra broker (authd-msentraid) is NOT - it is a
# Canonical snap, and seeding snaps into a live-build image is unsolved here.
# See installer/README.md.
authd

# --- .NET (README: Core, non-negotiable, both modes) --------------------------
# resolute ships .NET 10, not 9. Canonical packages this now; it does not come
# from packages.microsoft.com any more.
#
# THE RUNTIME, NOT THE SDK, since 2026-08-25 - C2 in
# docs/CURATION-AND-DELIVERY-PLAN.md §4.1. Nothing in the image needs a
# compiler: os7-setup is NativeAOT and runs with .NET deleted (spike S2,
# measured), and PowerShell 7 is the self-contained upstream tarball hook 0020
# installs. The SDK was serving a product intention rather than a dependency,
# and it brought 216 MiB of llvm and clang in behind a Recommends
# (dotnet-sdk-aot-10.0) that nobody chose.
#
# The runtime stays because the Foundation Framework (C3) is a .NET library and
# set of services, so the product will have a first-party consumer for it.
# Installed-Size in the pinned archive: sdk 355 MiB against runtime 79 MiB plus
# aspnetcore 26 MiB.
dotnet-runtime-10.0
aspnetcore-runtime-10.0

# --- What Setup needs to install the system ----------------------------------
# From installer/SETUP-PLAN.md 7.1. These are needed at INSTALL time, so they
# must be on the ISO; the D3 group below must also end up on the INSTALLED
# system or it will not boot.
squashfs-tools
rsync
gdisk
dosfstools
efibootmgr
shim-signed
kbd
console-setup

# --- D3: LUKS2 under ZFS -----------------------------------------------------
# Intune recognises only dm-crypt, so encryption is LUKS2 beneath the pool
# rather than ZFS native. cryptsetup-initramfs is what actually unlocks rpool at
# boot - without it an installed system stops at the initramfs prompt.
cryptsetup
cryptsetup-initramfs
tpm2-tools

# --- D4: swap ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Swap must not live on ZFS.
systemd-zram-generator

# --- Network: screen 9 -------------------------------------------------------
# netplan.io and systemd-resolved are already in the image via ubuntu-standard,
# and are what os7-setup writes for (SETUP-PLAN 7.2). These three are NOT, on
# arm64: the amd64 image gets them transitively through network-manager, which
# arm64 never installs because it is server-only.
#
# Without wpasupplicant, screen 9W cannot associate on arm64 at all. `iw` is
# what scans, and `rfkill` is what notices a hardware kill switch instead of
# reporting a radio that simply never answers.
#
# The WIRELESS FIRMWARE is already on both images - 19 linux-firmware packages
# covering Intel, Broadcom, Realtek, MediaTek, Qualcomm and Marvell. That is the
# part that is large and that cannot be fetched without the network it is needed
# for, and it is paid for already.
#
# NOTE FOR SPIKE S7: naming these explicitly puts them in
# /usr/lib/os7/packages.manifest on BOTH architectures, so the manifest changes
# with this commit. That is a deliberate change of S7's comparison baseline, not
# drift between two builds.
wpasupplicant
iw
rfkill

# --- Backup: sanoid and syncoid (docs/BACKUP-PLAN.md) -------------------------
# One package, three programs: /usr/sbin/sanoid takes and thins snapshots on a
# policy, /usr/sbin/syncoid replicates them with zfs send/receive, and findoid
# is there and unused (BACKUP-PLAN B10 says why).
#
# GPL-3.0+, and shelled out to as ordinary programs rather than vendored, so
# OS/7's own MIT licensing is unaffected. It is `Architecture: all` - pure perl -
# which is why this line is in the COMMON list and needs no arch split.
#
# MEASURED against the pinned snapshot on 2026-08-25, not remembered:
#   sanoid 2.3.0-1, universe, 56 770 B, installed 213 KiB
#   SHA256 24bc2809f01eab894383b5a8a09f6346a9ad19280268928c167e04a4ae1d603d
# It pulls five more, all resolvable from the same pin: pv 1.10.3-1 and
# lzop 1.04-2build4 (main), mbuffer 20251025+ds1-1 (universe), and the perl
# libraries libconfig-inifiles-perl 3.000003-4build1 and libcapture-tiny-perl
# 0.50-1 (main, both arch:all). Roughly 357 KB downloaded, 1.1 MB installed.
# `perl` itself is already in the image via ubuntu-standard.
sanoid
# NOT a dependency of sanoid, and both programs need it: sanoid's lock check and
# syncoid's "is the target already receiving" check both run `ps`. Named here so
# that a base-system change which drops it fails the build rather than the first
# backup.
procps

# --- Base tooling ------------------------------------------------------------
openssh-server
curl
ca-certificates
gnupg
sudo
git
less
vim
